    "created_at": "2017-10-06T13:15:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-06T13:15:16Z",
    "body": "For what it's worth, one more alternative I can think of is emitting an end tag token with an empty tag name in that case.\r\n\r\nAdvantage: This would be fully backwards compatible since tokenizer is an internal detail and not exposed to the user, and any mismatching end tag names are already ignored by the tree builder (unless I'm mistaken).\r\n\r\nDisadvantage: Emitting a bogus token seems more consistent with what we do for other invalid end tag productions (e.g. `</ >` where the only difference with `</>` is a whitespace).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
